{
    "background_story": "Wesson was a former Marine who had honed his instincts on the battlefield. After leaving the military, he became a search and rescue operative, using his skills to locate missing people in the wilderness. Wesson's ability to trust his instincts often proved to be the difference between life and death. One fateful day, he was tasked with finding a young girl who had wandered away from her family's campsite. As he combed through the dense forest, Wesson's instincts told him to follow a narrow stream, despite the lack of obvious signs. His gut led him to a small cave, where he found the shivering girl, huddled in the corner. Wesson's instinctive decision had saved her life, and he continued to rely on his intuition to guide him in his critical work.",
